---
title: Status and roadmap
summary: What is built and tested, what is deliberately out of scope so far, and the open gaps, ordered by the algorithms they block.
order: 5
---

## Built and tested

- Model building over typed quantities on flat and curved manifolds (SO(3), SE(3)), including
  discrete quantities.
- Evaluation of $\log p$, $\log q$ and the log-weight; first-order derivatives and Hessian–vector
  products.
- Bindings, and the readers built on them: `residual_layout`, `information*`, `GaussianBlock`,
  `coverage`.
- The Gaussian, with a Fisher root, and joint Gaussian factors.
- A compiler with an epoch-keyed cache, cut compilation, and slot liveness.
- Host `f64` dense factorizations.

## Open gaps

| Gap | Blocks |
| --- | --- |
| No RNG seeding; no per-quantity sampling | Reproducible MCMC/SMC; per-chain streams |
| No derivatives of $q$ or of the weight | Gradient-based variational inference |
| Fisher assembly is not tape-differentiable | Riemannian-manifold HMC |
| No block-sparse $J$, no sparse solvers | Large models |
| No Schur complement / marginal precision | The computational half of marginalization |
| No estimator, line search, or convergence test | Every deterministic estimator |
| No `hessian_*` assembly | Newton methods; observed information |
| No residual-vector assembly matching `jacobian_*` | Least-squares steps must hand-roll $r$ |
| Joint proposals over several quantities | Block proposals |
| Deferred bindings | Expensive-root families; very large models |

Details are in `docs/skoro.md` §5 and `docs/roadmap.md` in the repository.

